  "title": "Why Your Pull-Ups Aren\u0027t Increasing",
  "hook": "Stuck at the same number of pull-ups for months?",
  "targetDurationSeconds": 30.599999999999998,
  "narrationText": "Stuck at the same number of pull-ups for months? Doing max sets every day feels productive, but it wears you down. Use slow negatives: lower yourself for three to five seconds. Your lats do most of the pulling. Half reps build half strength; full range builds all of it. Train three days a week, add one rep at a time, and sleep well. Most people add a rep every week or two. Rest days are when the muscle actually adapts.",
